SUMMARY:Island Beach State Park
DESCRIPTION:Search maritime forest for migrant vireos\, tanagers\, and warblers. We’ll also spend time checking out waterbirds in the marshes. Spring birding at one the state’s most beautiful parks. We’ll look for migrant songbirds and survey bayside wetlands for a variety of waterbirds including herons\, ibis\, and terns. We’ll meet just outside of the park entrance\, in the median parking lot at the end of Rt. 35. There is a $5 entry fee to the park if you don’t have a state park pass or are less than 62 years old. Be prepared for a good amount of walking over flat and sandy terrain. Led by Scott Barnes and Linda Mack. \nA NOTE ON MEETING LOCATION! We’ll meet just outside of the park entrance\, in the median parking lot at the end of Rt. 35. \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nWEATHER & TRANSPORTATION: Please arrive at the appointed time. Be sure to check the forecast in advance and dress in layers appropriate for prevailing weather conditions. We sometimes bird in the rain\, so bring rain gear if warranted. Transportation during the field trip is by private vehicle (be sure you have enough gas). Most trips involve some amount of walking\, sometimes through muddy or sandy terrain. \nCANCELLATION: NJA/CMBO programs require a minimum number of registrants to run\, five days in advance of the start of the tour but are seldom cancelled. If we do cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, we notify all participants in advance\, and all are eligible for a full credit or refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 30 days in advance. Cancellations 10 to 30 days in advance may be subject to a 25% service charge. No refunds or credits for cancellations less than ten days in advance unless due to health emergencies. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/island-beach-state-park-19/
LOCATION:NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Island-Beach-State-Park.jpg
END:VEVENT
